dels, Destroy traditional aesthetics, Unavailable to micro - clusters, Technology gap, Context - appropriate tools, Ergonomic, Semi - mechanized yarn winders, Temperature - controlled, Eco - friendly dye baths, Eco - friendly processing, Increase average monthly income, 50%, MSME cooperative, Post - grant, Phulkari preservation model, Cooperative model, Master trainers, Usage fee, Buy - back agreements, MSME cooperative model, Scalable blueprint, State backing, Regional textile clusters\n- This section must cover: after the proposed technological solution is proven, how it will be scaled up or taken forward- whether by involving State Government for large scale technology dissemination or via market or any other means – any entrepreneur or business person can be involved in any manner?\n\nSECTION BRIEF:\n- Section: Possibility of replication of project in similar areas\n- Purpose: after the proposed technological solution is proven, how it will be scaled up or taken forward- whether by involving State Government for large scale technology dissemination or via market or any other means – any entrepreneur or business person can be involved in any manner?\n- Reviewer intent: after the proposed technological solution is proven, how it will be scaled up or taken forward- whether by involving State Government for large scale technology dissemination or via market or any other means – any entrepreneur or business person can be involved in any manner?\n- Word budget: 50\n- Proposal thesis: The proposal establishes a fundable program for science and technology, socio-economic development, capacity enhancement by combining a credible delivery model, measurable outcomes, and clear alignment with STI Hubs.\n- Central objective: Prepare PART 3: PROBLEM IDENTIFICATION AND PROPOSED S&T INTERVENTIONS.\n- Key contributions: Scale, burden, or urgency of PART 3: PROBLEM IDENTIFICATION AND PROPOSED S&T INTERVENTIONS: Consolidates the problem and solution into the core Part 3 narrative.