le inventive concept' standard", "Claims must be clear and succinct per s.40(3)"], "constraints": ["Each claim as single sentence", "Multiple dependent claims permitted (including on other multiple dependents)", "Claims must be fairly based on disclosed matter", "All claims relate to single inventive concept"], "instruction": "Draft claims compliant with Section 40 of the Patents Act 1990. Claims must be clear, succinct, and fairly based on description."}, "constraints": ["Use 'comprising' as the default open transitional term unless a closed scope is specifically required.", "Draft each claim as a single sentence.", "Dependent claims may refer to one or more previous claims, including other multiple dependent claims.", "All claim features must be supported by the description of embodiments and define a single inventive concept."], "instruction": "Draft a full set of claims compliant with Australian patent practice."}, "summary": {"topUp": {"additions": ["Structure: problem → solution → advantages"], "constraints": ["Align with independent claims scope", "Use flexible language ('in embodiments', 'according to aspects')", "Include brief statement of advantages"], "instruction": "Per IP Australia practice, draft a Summary stating technical problem, inventive solution, and advantageous effects."}, "constraints": ["Outline the technical problem, the solution provided by the invention and its advantageous effects.", "Ensure consistency with the independent claims."], "instruction": "Draft the Summary of the Invention section."}, "abstract": {"topUp": {"additions": ["IP Australia may amend abstracts exceeding 150 words", "Reference most illustrative figure if drawings present"], "constraints": ["50-150 words preferred, max 150", "Single paragraph", "Technical summary only—no advantages/marketing", "Enable quick understanding of field and main features"], "instruction": "Per IP Australia guidelines, draft an Abstract of 50-150 words summarizing technical disclosure."}, "co