cmojsz3a4001sc2dds7ip151i	cmojscwzg000qc2dddwzxvepc	problem_definition	assistant	I see you're asking for topic ideas based on your LLM expertise. That's a starting point, but STI Hubs requires a specific problem tied to a target community, with evidence of scale and urgency. Instead of listing topics, let's nail down the problem you want to solve.\n\n**What's missing:** A concrete problem statement, target population, location, and urgency signal aligned with the call's focus on socio-economic development, livelihoods, or Indigenous Knowledge Systems.\n\nReviewers will reject a generic proposal. Let me suggest two focused bundles that combine your LLM skills with call priorities. Please pick one or modify – each gives us enough to start drafting.	\N	brainstorm_marker_v1	valid	0	[]	problem_core	[]	[{"level": "gentle_redirect", "message": "Please move from generic 'topic ideas' to a specific problem statement with target population, location, and quantified scale. The options above show what reviewer-ready looks like.", "pointKey": "problem_core"}]	{}	[{"text": "I approve this bundle: Core problem: Smallholder farmers in [District, State] lack real-time, vernacular crop advisory on pest/disease management, leading to 30–40% post-harvest loss (source: district agri report 2023). Scale: 500,000 farmers affected, annual loss ~₹200 crore. Urgency: Climate change is accelerating new pest patterns; existing helplines are understaffed. Target community: Tribal and SC/ST marginal farmers, average income ₹40,000/year, with limited smartphone literacy. Root cause: No AI-powered local-language decision support system. Direct beneficiaries: 50,000 farmers in first year. Proposed S&T intervention: LLM-based multilingual chatbot trained on ICAR datasets and local crop calendars. This is a new, low-cost adaptive solution surpassing state-run IVRS systems (which have <15% adoption).", "label": "A", "covers": [{"label": "Core problem statement", "pointKey": "problem_core", "stageKey":