5], "recognizing": [142], "significant": [139], "traditional": [8, 102, 112, 151], "(Traditional": [95], "expressions,": [10], "expressions.": [153], "intellectual": [14, 118, 122], "intersection": [5], "investigated": [42], "preservation": [49], "Registration,": [154], "collaborative": [11, 44]}, "cited_by_percentile_year": {"max": 99, "min": 94}, "corresponding_author_ids": ["https://openalex.org/A5002622037"], "countries_distinct_count": 1, "institutions_distinct_count": 1, "corresponding_institution_ids": ["https://openalex.org/I157614274"], "sustainable_development_goals": [{"id": "https://metadata.un.org/sdg/5", "score": 0.6700000166893005, "display_name": "Gender equality"}], "citation_normalized_percentile": {"value": 0.99549458, "is_in_top_1_percent": true, "is_in_top_10_percent": true}}, "abstract": "Abstract This article considers the intersection of gender, traditional cultural expressions, collaborative innovation, and intellectual property in the Tonga Indigenous community of Zambia. Based on a study of the Tonga rural women basket makers who are organized around craft clubs, the study investigated the collaborative environment that fosters the preservation of the cultural tradition of basket weaving, the impact it has had on empowering the women, and the legal protection options available for the Tonga baskets. The study found that Zambia’s 2016 Protection of Traditional Knowledge, Genetic Resources and Expressions of Folklore Act no. 16 (Traditional Knowledge Act) gives automatic protection to traditional cultural expressions and the option for the protection of traditional cultural expressions under the existing intellectual property laws. Though intellectual property protection may not be practical for the Tonga baskets, the Traditional Knowledge Act is a significant step in recognizing the customary values and governance principles in protecting traditional cultural expressions. Registration, in terms of the Traditional Knowledge Act, could enhance the recognition of the baskets, preserve and promote the cultural heritage, and empower the Tonga women.", "publisher": "Cambridge University Press", "citationCount": 17, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Intellectual property", "Traditional knowledge", "Craft", "Folklore", "Intangible cultural heritage"], "publicationDate": "2022-02-01", "publicationType": "journal-article", "journalAbbreviation": "International Journal of Cultural Property"}, {"id": "oa_W4221094666", "doi": "10.1007/s10606-022-09425-8", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10606-022-09425-8", "issn": "0925-9724", "year": 2022, "issue": "2", "pages": "237-297", "title": "People First, Data Second: A Humanitarian Research Framework for Fieldwork with Refugees by War Zones", "venue": "Computer Supported Cooperative Work (CSCW)", "pdfUrl": "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10606-022-09425-8.pdf", "source": "openalex", "volume": "31", "authors": ["Karen Fisher"], "rawData": {"id": "https://openalex.org/W4221094666", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10606-022-09425-8", "ids": {"doi": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10606-022-09425-8", "pmid": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35345597", "openalex": "https://openalex.org/W4221094666"}, "fwci": 1.3795, "mesh": [], "type": "article", "title": "People First, Data Second: A Humanitarian Research Framework for Fieldwork with Refugees by War Zones", "awards": [], "biblio": {"issue": "2", "volume": "31", "last_page": "297", "first_page": "237"}, "topics": [{"id": "https://openalex.org/T10803", "field": {"id": "https://openalex.org/fields/17", "display_name": "Computer Science"}, "score": 0.9998999834060669, "domain": {"id": "https://openalex.org/domains/3", "display_name": "Physical Sciences"}, "subfield": {"id": "https://openalex.org/subfields/1709", "display_name": "Human-Computer Interaction"}, "display_name": "Innovative Human-Technology Interaction"}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/T13194", "field": {"id": "https://openalex.org/fields/17", "display_name": "Computer Sc