ers learn, socialize, and collaborate in a networked three-dimensional (3D) immersive virtual world. Due to the rich multimedia streaming capability and immersive user experience with high-speed communication, the metaverse is an ideal model for education, training, and skill development tasks. To facilitate research in this area, we provide a comprehensive review of the various educational use cases and explore how enabling technologies such as Extended reality (XR) and the Internet of Everything (IoE) will play a major role in educational services in future metaverses. Secondly, we provide an overview of metaverse-based educational applications focusing on education, training, and skill development and analyze the technologies they are built upon. We identify common research problems and future research directions in the domain. The paper also identifies core ethical considerations of metaverse for education and potential pitfalls. We believe this survey can fully demonstrate the versatility of metaverse-driven education, which could serve as a potential guideline for the researchers.", "publisher": "Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers", "citationCount": 120, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer science", "The Internet", "Multimedia", "Virtual reality", "World Wide Web"], "publicationDate": "2024-01-01", "publicationType": "journal-article", "journalAbbreviation": "IEEE Transactions on Learning Technologies"}, {"id": "oa_W3184502676", "doi": "10.1007/s10606-021-09398-0", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10606-021-09398-0", "issn": "0925-9724", "year": 2021, "issue": "2", "pages": "159-196", "title": "Challenges and Paradoxes in Decolonising HCI: A Critical Discussion", "venue": "Computer Supported Cooperative Work (CSCW)", "pdfUrl": "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10606-021-09398-0.pdf", "source": "openalex", "volume": "31", "authors": ["Shaimaa Lazem", "Danilo Giglitto", "Makuochi Nkwo", "Hafeni Mthoko", "Jessica Upani", "Anicia Peters"], "ra