": [59], "confront": [111], "emerging": [112], "features": [143], "literacy": [27, 53, 117], "radical,": [12], "societal": [7], "Semiotics": [94], "Unsworth,": [108], "digitally": [36], "embodied,": [33], "framework": [22], "knowledge": [30], "literacy.": [16, 101], "mediated.": [37], "organised": [79], "practice.": [149], "scholars,": [69], "teachers,": [68], "today’s": [39], "addressing": [29], "curriculum": [61], "landscape,": [52], "practices.": [118], "readers’": [98], "understood": [58], "educational": [51, 146], "established": [60, 124], "materiality": [131], "multimodal,": [34], "researchers": [71, 125], "structures.": [65], "Materiality;": [86], "implications": [136], "professional": [148], "technological": [42], "understanding": [14, 99], "unprecedented": [1], "breakthroughs,": [43], "technological,": [5], "contextualised,": [32], "next-generation": [115], "recommendations": [144], "interdisciplinary": [105]}, "cited_by_percentile_year": {"max": 100, "min": 97}, "corresponding_author_ids": ["https://openalex.org/A5076819534"], "countries_distinct_count": 1, "institutions_distinct_count": 3, "corresponding_institution_ids": ["https://openalex.org/I86695891"], "sustainable_development_goals": [{"id": "https://metadata.un.org/sdg/4", "score": 0.8399999737739563, "display_name": "Quality Education"}], "citation_normalized_percentile": {"value": 0.99910674, "is_in_top_1_percent": true, "is_in_top_10_percent": true}}, "abstract": "The unprecedented rate of global, technological, and societal change calls for a radical, new understanding of literacy. This book offers a nuanced framework for making sense of literacy by addressing knowledge as contextualised, embodied, multimodal, and digitally mediated. In today’s world of technological breakthroughs, social shifts, and rapid changes to the educational landscape, literacy can no longer be understood through established curriculum and static text structures. To prepare teachers, scholars, and researchers for the digital future, the book is organised around three themes – Mind and Materiality; Body and Senses; and Texts and Digital Semiotics – to shape readers’ understanding of literacy. Opening up new interdisciplinary themes, Mills, Unsworth, and Scholes confront emerging issues for next-generation digital literacy practices. The volume helps new and established researchers rethink dynamic changes in the materiality of texts and their implications for the mind and body, and features recommendations for educational and professional practice.", "citationCount": 63, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Futures contract", "Literacy", "Computer science", "Sociology", "Economics"], "publicationDate": "2022-08-18", "publicationType": "book"}]	{"removedResultIds": ["oa_W4385663911", "oa_W2823189734", "oa_W4391248986", "oa_W3184502676", "oa_W4225002570", "oa_W4225000370", "oa_W3159031910", "oa_W4395470353", "oa_W4378575123", "oa_W4300480973"]}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-04-29 11:04:03.688	2026-04-29 11:08:16.996	\N
cmojy7q4100dw77yct47tc3n0	cmojtx277009k77ycv5pu74az	traditional knowledge digital library TKDL Maori database critique	{crossref,openalex,semantic_scholar}	2018	\N	[{"id": "cr_10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7", "doi": "10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7", "issn": "0957-8536", "year": 2021, "issue": "1", "pages": "1-19", "title": "India’s Traditional Knowledge Digital Library and the Politics of Patent Classifications", "venue": "Law and Critique", "pdfUrl": "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7.pdf", "source": "crossref", "volume": "34", "authors": ["Fredriksson, Martin"], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7", "ISSN": ["0957-8536", "1572-8617"], "link": [{"URL": "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7.pdf", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7/fulltext.html", "content-type": "text/html", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7.pdf", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "page": "1-19", "type": "journal-article", "issue": "1", "score": 32.474663, "title": ["India’s Traditional Knowledge Digital Library and the Politics of Patent Classifications"], "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3309-3840", "given": "Martin", "family": "Fredriksson", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}], "funder": [{"id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100000781", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}], "DOI": "10.13039/501100000781", "name": "European Research Council", "award": ["741095-PASSIMERC- 2016-AdG"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["741095-PASSIMERC- 2016-AdG"]}], "doi-asserted-by": "publisher"}, {"id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100003945", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "crossref"}], "DOI": "10.13039/501100003945", "name": "Linköping University", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref"}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2021, 6, 12]]}, "member": "297", "prefix": "10.1007", "source": "Crossref", "volume": "34", "created": {"date-time": "2021-06-12T21:02:44Z", "timestamp": 1623531764000, "date-parts": [[2021, 6, 12]]}, "indexed": {"version": "3.50.1", "date-time": "2026-03-26T09:34:54Z", "timestamp": 1774517694248, "date-parts": [[2026, 3, 26]]}, "license": [{"URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0", "start": {"date-time": "2021-06-12T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1623456000000, "date-parts": [[2021, 6, 12]]}, "delay-in-days": 0, "content-version": "tdm"}, {"URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0", "start": {"date-time": "2021-06-12T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1623456000000, "date-parts": [[2021, 6, 12]]}, "delay-in-days": 0, "content-version": "vor"}], "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title><jats:p>This article analyzes India’s Traditional Knowledge Digital Library (TKDL) as a potential intervention in the administration of patent law. The TKDL is a database including a vast body of traditional medical knowledge from India, aiming to prevent the patenting and misappropriation of that knowledge. This article contextualizes the TKDL in relation to documentation theory as well as to existing research on the uses of databases to protect traditional knowledge. It explores the TKDL’s potential consequences for India’s traditional medical knowledge and the wider implications that traditional knowledge databases can have for the safeguarding of traditional knowledge in general. The article concludes that on the one hand the TKDL bridges the gap between the main branches of Indian traditional medicine and the formal knowledge system of International Patent Classifications. Furthermore, it has also inspired revisions of the International Patent Classification system, which makes it better adapted to incorporate traditional medical knowledge. On the other hand, critical research on traditional knowledge documentation argues that traditional knowledge databases, like the TKDL, can decontextualize the knowledge they catalogue and dispossess its original owners. The TKDL, however, also fits into a national, Indian agenda of documenting and modernizing traditional medicine that predates the formation of the TKDL by several decades and challenges the dichotomy between traditional and scientific knowledge systems that originally motivated the formation of the TKDL.</jats:p>", "language": "en", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://link.springer.com/10.1007/s10978-021-09299-7"}}, "assertion": [{"name": "accepted", "group": {"name": "ArticleHistory", "label": "Article History"}, "label": "Accepted", "order": 1, "value": "25 May 2021"}, {"name": "first_online", "group": {"name": "ArticleHistory", "label": "Article History"}, "label": "First Online", "order": 2, "value": "12 June 2021"}], "deposited": {"date-time": "2024-09-01T18:41:07Z", "timestamp": 1725216067000, "date-parts": [[2024, 9, 1]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "0957-8536"}, {"type": "electronic", "value": "1572-8617"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2021, 6, 12]]}, "publisher": "Springer Science and Business Media LLC", "reference": [{"DOI": "10.1016/S0172-2190(00)00073-9", "key": "9299_CR1", "year": "2000", "author": "Stephen Adams", "volume": "22", "first-page": "291", "unstructured": "Adams, Stephen. 2000. Using the international patent classification in an online environment. World Patent Information 22: 291–300.", "journal-title": "World Patent Information", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher"}, {"DOI": "10.1515/9780823276387", "key": "9299_CR2", "year": "2017", "author": "Melissa Adler", "unstructured": "Adler, Melissa. 2017. Cruising the library: Perversities in the organization of knowledge. New York: Fordham University Press.", "volume-tit