the north. Oslo: Spartacus Forlag; 2000. p. 37–44.", "volume-title": "Responding to bio-prospecting: from biodiversity in the south to medicines in the north"}, {"key": "38_CR18", "unstructured": "National Knowledge Commission. Traditional knowledge. 2005. http://knowledgecommissionarchive.nic.in/focus/traditional.asp . Accessed 25 Aug 2016."}, {"key": "38_CR19", "year": "2004", "author": "S Twarog", "unstructured": "Twarog S, Kapoor P. Protecting and promoting traditional knowledge: systems, national experiences and international dimensions. In: United Nations Conference on Trade and Development. New York and Geneva: United Nations; 2004.. http://unctad.org/en/docs/ditcted10_en.pdf . Accessed 21 Aug 2016.", "volume-title": "United Nations Conference on Trade and Development"}, {"DOI": "10.1093/jiplp/jpm144", "key": "38_CR20", "year": "2007", "author": "V Vadi", "volume": "2", "first-page": "682", "unstructured": "Vadi V. Intangible heritage: traditional medicine and knowledge governance. J Intellect Prop Law Pract. 2007;2:682–91.", "journal-title": "J Intellect Prop Law Pract", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher"}, {"DOI": "10.3164/jcbn.2007001", "key": "38_CR21", "year": "2007", "author": "AD Vaidya", "volume": "41", "first-page": "1", "unstructured": "Vaidya AD, Devasagayam TP. Current status of herbal drugs in India: an overview. J Clin Biochem Nutr. 2007;41:1–11.", "journal-title": "J Clin Biochem Nutr", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher"}, {"key": "38_CR22", "year": "2003", "author": "WHO Traditional medicine. Secretariat", "unstructured": "WHO Traditional medicine. Secretariat. World Health Organization Fifty-Sixth World Health Assembly A56/18. Geneva: World Health Organization; 2003.. http://apps.who.int/gb/archive/pdf_files/WHA56/ea5618.pdf . Accessed 6 May 2016", "volume-title": "World Health Organization Fifty-Sixth World Health Assembly A56/18"}, {"key": "38_CR23", "unstructured": "World Health Organization. Traditional medicine – growing needs and potential. 2002. http://whqlibdoc.who.int/hq/2002/WHO_EDM_2002.4.pdf . Accessed 13 Jun 2017."}, {"key": "38_CR24", "year": "2004", "author": "X Zhang", "unstructured": "Zhang X. Traditional medicine: its importance and protection. Protecting and promoting traditional knowledge: systems, national experiences and international dimensions. New York: United Nations; 2004.. http://unctad.org/en/docs/ditcted10_en.pdf . Accessed 8 Jul 2017", "volume-title": "Traditional medicine: its importance and protection. Protecting and promoting traditional knowledge: systems, national experiences and international dimensions"}], "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1007/springer_crossmark_policy", "content-domain": {"domain": ["link.springer.com"], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "container-title": ["Herbal Medicine in India"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2020]]}, "reference-count": 24, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 9, 11]]}, "references-count": 24, "publisher-location": "Singapore", "is-referenced-by-count": 2}, "publisher": "Springer Singapore", "citationCount": 2, "publicationDate": "2020", "publicationPlace": "Singapore"}, {"id": "cr_10.29121/shodhkosh.v4.i2.2023.4333", "doi": "10.29121/shodhkosh.v4.i2.2023.4333", "url": "https://doi.org/10.29121/shodhkosh.v4.i2.2023.4333", "issn": "2582-7472", "year": 2023, "issue": "2", "title": "THE ROLE OF TRADITIONAL KNOWLEDGE DIGITAL LIBRARY IN PROTECTION OF INDIAN TRADITIONAL KNOWLEDGE: A CRITICAL ANALYSIS", "venue": "ShodhKosh: Journal of Visual and Performing Arts", "pdfUrl": "https://www.granthaalayahpublication.org/Arts-Journal/ShodhKosh/article/download/4333/3939", "source": "crossref", "volume": "4", "authors": ["Manjari Chandra,", "Shabran, Rohit P"], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.29121/shodhkosh.v4.i2.2023.4333", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.29121/shodhkosh.v4.i2.2023.4333", "ISSN": ["2582-7472"], "link": [{"URL": "https://www.granthaalayahpublication.org/Arts-Journal/ShodhKosh/article/download/4333/3939", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://www.granthaalayahpublication.org/Arts-Journal/ShodhKosh/article/download/4333/3939", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "type": "journal-article", "issue": "2", "score": 27.115145, "title": ["THE ROLE OF TRADITIONAL KNOWLEDGE DIGITAL LIBRARY IN PROTECTION OF INDIAN TRADITIONAL KNOWLEDGE: A CRITICAL ANALYSIS"], "author": [{"family": "Manjari Chandra", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Rohit P", "family": "Shabran", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2023, 12, 31]]}, "member": "11657", "prefix": "10.29121", "source": "Crossref", "volume": "4", "created": {"date-time": "2025-02-28T09:12:19Z", "timestamp": 1740733939000, "date-parts": [[2025, 2, 28]]}, "indexed": {"version": "3.50.1", "date-time": "2026-04-06T16:54:36Z", "timestamp": 1775494476702, "date-parts": [[2026, 4, 6]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>This research analyzes the pivotal role of Traditional Knowledge Digital Libraries (TKDLs) in safeguarding Indian traditional knowledge, critically analyzing their impact on preservation, accessibility, and legal protection. Examining the key features and functionalities of existing TKDLs, we assess their effectiveness in documenting and disseminating traditional knowledge. The study delves into the legal and policy frameworks at national and international levels, evaluating their support and potential hindrances to utilizing TKDLs for protection. Additionally, we explore the extent to which these digital repositories empower indigenous communities and practitioners while respecting cultural sensitivities and intellectual property rights. Challenges in digitization and management of traditional knowledge are scrutinized, seeking solutions for ethical considerations. The research also gauges stakeholder perspectives, including those of indigenous communities, policymakers, researchers, and legal experts, to understand the perceived effectiveness and relevance of TKDLs. This paper covers a number of topics related to the Traditional Knowledge Digital Library of India (TKDL), such as its contribution to the preservation of traditional knowledge, safeguarding and disseminating traditional knowledge, the database's current status, advantages of TKDL, instances of bio-piracy of Indian traditional knowledge, and the organization's most notable accomplishments in this area.</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.granthaalayahpublication.org/Arts-Journal/ShodhKosh/article/view/4333"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2025-02-28T09:12:28Z", "timestamp": 1740733948000, "date-parts": [[2025, 2, 28]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "electronic", "value": "2582-7472"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2023, 12, 31]]}, "publisher": "Granthaalayah Publications and Printers", "reference": [{"key": "65640", "unstructured": "Gupta V. K. “Traditional knowledge Digital Library”, Sub-Regional experts Meeting in Asia on Intangible cultural heritage, Bangkok, Thailand, 13-16 December 2005. (Conference Proceedings)"}, {"key": "65641", "unstructured": "http://www.accu.or.jp/ich/en/pdf/c2005sub_reg_Ind/pdf (Viewed on 11 January 2023)"}, {"key": "65642", "unstructured": "http://www.bc.edu/schools/law/lawreviews/meta-elements/journals/bciclr/27/12FMS.htm"}, {"key": "65643", "unstructured": "(Viewed on 13 January 2024)"}, {"key": "65644", "unstructured": "http://www.indiatogether.org/ (Viewed on 13 January 2023)"}, {"key": "65645", "unstructured": "http://www.knowledgecommission.gov.in/recommendations/traditional1.asp (viewed on 10"}, {"key": "65646", "unstructured": "January 2024)"}, {"key": "65647", "unstructured": "http://www.tkdl.res.in/tkdl/langdefault/common/TKRC.asp (Viewed on 13 January 2024)"}, {"key": "65648", "unstructured": "IPRs.” www.parl.gc.ca/information/library/PRBpubs (Viewed on 13 January 2024)"}, {"key": "65649", "unstructured": "Martin van Ameijde, “Biopiracy: The need for a protective solution?” http://www.jur.lu.se/Internet/Utbildning/kurser/JCA803.nsf/43e828219552/ (Viewed on 11 January 2023)"}, {"key": "65650", "unstructured": "Menon Ramesh. “Traditional Knowledge receives a boost from the government”, India Together,"}, {"key": "65651", "unstructured": "National Knowledge Commission, 2005. “Traditional Knowledge”"}, {"key": "65652", "unstructured": "Simeone Tonina, “Indigenous traditional knowledge and"}, {"key": "65653", "unstructured": "Subbiah Sumati. “Reaping what they sow. The Basmati rice controversy and strategies for protecting TK”"}, {"key": "65654", "unstructured": "TKDL-Traditional Knowledge Digital Library www.tkdl.res.in (viewed on 10 January 2024)"}, {"key": "65655", "unstructured": "Traditional Knowledge Resource Classification"}, {"key": "65656", "unstructured": "Yoga piracy: India shows who’s the guru http://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/Yoga-piracy- India-shows-whosthe-guru/articleshow/4167939.cms (viewed on 10 January 2024)"}], "journal-issue": {"issue": "2", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2023, 7, 19]]}}, "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.29121/shodhkosh-crossmark-policy", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "container-title": ["ShodhKosh: Journal of Visual and Performing Arts"], "reference-count": 17, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2023, 12, 31]]}, "references-count": 17, "short-container-title": ["ShodhKosh J. Vis. Per. Arts"], "is-referenced-by-count": 1}, "abstract": "<jats:p>This research analyzes the pivotal role of Traditional Knowledge Digital Libraries (TKDLs) in safeguarding Indian traditional knowledge, critically analyzing their impact on preservation, accessibility, and legal protection. Examining the key features and functionalities of existing TKDLs, we assess their effectiveness in documenting and disseminating traditional knowledge. The study delves into the legal and policy frameworks at national and international levels, evaluating their support and potential hindrances to utilizing TKDLs for protection. Additionally, we explore the extent to which these digital repositories empower indigenous communities and practitioners while respecting cultural sensitivities and intellectual property rights. Challenges in digitization and management of traditional knowledge are scrutinized, seeking solutions for ethical considerations. The research also gauges stakeholder perspectives, including those of indigenous communities, policymakers, researchers, and legal experts, to understand the perceived effectiveness and relevance of TKDLs. This paper covers a number of topics related to the Traditional Knowledge Digital Library of India (TKDL), such as its contribution to the preservation of traditional knowledge, safeguarding and disseminating traditional knowledge, the database's current status, advantages of TKDL, instances of bio-piracy of Indian traditional knowledge, and the organization's most notable accomplishments in this area.</jats:p>", "publisher": "Granthaalayah Publications and Printers", "citationCount": 1, "publicationDate": "2023-12-31", "journalAbbreviation": "ShodhKosh J. Vis. Per. Arts"}, {"id": "oa_W2990595583", "doi": "10.12681/eadd/45962", "url": "https://doi.org/10.12681/eadd/45962", "year": 2019, "title": "Άυλη πολιτιστική κληρονομιά", "source": "openalex", "authors": ["Αντωνία Κορκά"], "rawData": {"id": "https://openalex.org/W2990595583", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.12681/eadd/45962", "ids": {"doi": "https://doi.org/10.12681/eadd/45962", "mag": "2990595583", "openalex": "https://openalex.org/W2990595583"}, "fwci": null, "mesh": [], "type": "dissertation", "title": "Άυλη πολιτιστική κληρονομιά", "awards": [], "biblio": {"issue": null, "volume": null, "last_page": null, "first_page": null}, "topics": [{"id": "https://openalex.org/T10055", "field": {"id": "https://openalex.org/fields/33", "display_name": "Social Sciences"}, "score": 0.9732000231742859,