nteado, Ana"], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.4894478", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4894478", "type": "posted-content", "score": 26.236477, "title": ["The Case of Patent Disclosure Requirements for Genetic Resources and Associated Traditional Knowledge, and the Custodianship of Traditional Knowledge -A Critique"], "author": [{"given": "Ana", "family": "Penteado", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "member": "78", "posted": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "prefix": "10.2139", "source": "Crossref", "created": {"date-time": "2024-07-17T15:40:56Z", "timestamp": 1721230856000, "date-parts": [[2024, 7, 17]]}, "indexed": {"date-time": "2024-07-18T00:20:56Z", "timestamp": 1721262056759, "date-parts": [[2024, 7, 18]]}, "subtype": "preprint", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=4894478"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2024-07-17T16:53:52Z", "timestamp": 1721235232000, "date-parts": [[2024, 7, 17]]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[2024]]}, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "reference": [{"key": "ref1", "volume": "3", "journal-title": "See United Nations Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples"}, {"key": "ref2", "author": "Wipo See", "journal-title": "WIPO Treaty on Intellectual Property, Genetic Resources, and Associated Traditional Knowledge"}], "group-title": "SSRN", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "reference-count": 2, "references-count": 2, "is-referenced-by-count": 0}, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "citationCount": 0, "publicationDate": "2024"}, {"id": "cr_10.69971/tipr.2.1.2024.20", "doi": "10.69971/tipr.2.1.2024.20", "url": "https://doi.org/10.69971/tipr.2.1.2024.20", "issn": "3007-8539", "year": 2024, "issue": "1", "title": "Traditional Knowledge Digital Library as Patent System Facilitator", "venue": "Trends in Intellectual Property Research", "pdfUrl": "https://iprtrends.com/TIPR/article/download/20/15", "source": "crossref", "volume": "2", "authors": ["Yadav, Alok Kumar", "Vibha,"], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.69971/tipr.2.1.2024.20", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.69971/tipr.2.1.2024.20", "ISSN": ["3007-8539", "3007-8520"], "link": [{"URL": "https://iprtrends.com/TIPR/article/download/20/15", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://iprtrends.com/TIPR/article/download/20/15", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "type": "journal-article", "issue": "1", "score": 25.713223, "title": ["Traditional Knowledge Digital Library as Patent System Facilitator"], "author": [{"given": "Alok Kumar", "family": "Yadav", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"family": "Vibha", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024, 11, 28]]}, "member": "50616", "prefix": "10.69971", "source": "Crossref", "volume": "2", "created": {"date-time": "2024-11-28T13:43:43Z", "timestamp": 1732801423000, "date-parts": [[2024, 11, 28]]}, "indexed": {"version": "3.30.0", "date-time": "2024-11-29T05:24:06Z", "timestamp": 1732857846662, "date-parts": [[2024, 11, 29]]}, "license": [{"URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/", "start": {"date-time": "2024-11-28T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1732752000000, "date-parts": [[2024, 11, 28]]}, "delay-in-days": 0, "content-version": "unspecified"}], "abstract": "<jats:p>The concept of the Traditional Knowledge Digital Library (TKDL) first emerged in India two decades ago. It upholds the current Indian patent law, which forbids the filing of patents based on traditional knowledge that is already in the public domain. Although, TKDL has been quite helpful in preserving traditional knowledge, it can be improved to maximize its potential. With tech advancements, it’s necessary to ensure that traditional knowledge is secured to facilitate the Intellectual Property regime, and prevent the exploitation of local customary knowledge. The primary issue concerning the current operational model is financial in nature. Many advocates strongly contend that access to the TKDL should be facilitated through commercialization. It is essential to grant access to the database to third parties to enhance awareness and promote indigenous knowledge systems. Allowing third-party access is therefore significantly beneficial from a financial perspective. In this regard, we have proposed the establishment of a TKDL fund, aimed at supporting various indigenous communities. This fund would generate financial returns from granting access, which would be distributed among indigenous communities and subsequently utilized for their development, thereby acknowledging their contributions in the realm of traditional knowledge.</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://iprtrends.com/TIPR/article/view/20"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2024-11-28T13:43:43Z", "timestamp": 1732801423000, "date-parts": [[2024, 11, 28]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "electronic", "value": "3007-8539"}, {"type": "print", "value": "3007-8520"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2024, 11, 28]]}, "publisher": "Innovative Insights (SMC-Private) Limited", "journal-issue": {"issue": "1", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2024, 11, 19]]}}, "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "container-title": ["Trends in Intellectual Property Research"], "reference-count": 0, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2024, 11, 28]]}, "references-count": 0, "short-container-title": ["Trend. Intellect. Prop. Res."], "is-referenced-by-count": 0}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The concept of the Traditional Knowledge Digital Library (TKDL) first emerged in India two decades ago. It upholds the current Indian patent law, which forbids the filing of patents based on traditional knowledge that is already in the public domain. Although, TKDL has been quite helpful in preserving traditional knowledge, it can be improved to maximize its potential. With tech advancements, it’s necessary to ensure that traditional knowledge is secured to facilitate the Intellectual Property regime, and prevent the exploitation of local customary knowledge. The primary issue concerning the current operational model is financial in nature. Many advocates strongly contend that access to the TKDL should be facilitated through commercialization. It is essential to grant access to the database to third parties to enhance awareness and promote indigenous knowledge systems. Allowing third-party access is therefore significantly beneficial from a financial perspective. In this regard, we have proposed the establishment of a TKDL fund, aimed at supporting various indigenous communities. This fund would generate financial returns from granting access, which would be distributed among indigenous communities and subsequently utilized for their development, thereby acknowledging their contributions in the realm of traditional knowledge.</jats:p>", "publisher": "Innovative Insights (SMC-Private) Limited", "citationCount": 0, "publicationDate": "2024-11-28", "journalAbbreviation": "Trend. Intellect. Prop. Res."}, {"id": "cr_10.65398/vkah1867", "doi": "10.65398/vkah1867", "url": "https://doi.org/10.65398/vkah1867", "isbn": "9788826610146", "year": 2025, "title": "India’s Experiences on Traditional Knowledge and Traditional Knowledge Digital Library (TKDL)", "venue": "Indigenous Peoples’ Knowledge and the Sciences: Combining Knowledge and Science on Vulnerabilities and Solutions for Resilience", "source": "crossref", "authors": ["Sattigeri, Viswajanani"], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.65398/vkah1867", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.65398/vkah1867", "ISBN": ["9788826610146"], "type": "book-chapter", "score": 46.54461, "title": ["India’s Experiences on Traditional Knowledge and Traditional Knowledge Digital Library (TKDL)"], "author": [{"given": "Viswajanani", "family": "Sattigeri", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "member": "54901", "prefix": "10.65398", "source": "Crossref", "created": {"date-time": "2025-12-09T10:07:15Z", "timestamp": 1765274835000, "date-parts": [[2025, 12, 9]]}, "indexed": {"version": "3.46.0", "date-time": "2025-12-09T10:11:18Z", "timestamp": 1765275078304, "date-parts": [[2025, 12, 9]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The workshop on “Indigenous Peoples’ Knowledge and the Sciences” organised by the Pontifical Academy of Sciences (PAS) and the Pontifical Academy of Social Sciences (PASS) focused on bringing together indigenous knowledge and local communities and the science fraternity to arrive at common understanding, objectives and joint work to address climate change vulnerabilities affecting lives and livelihoods. The workshop witnessed participation from across the world, and India shared its experiences on handling and working with traditional knowledge (TK) and the Traditional Knowledge Digital Library (TKDL). The importance of national government policies was highlighted in the context of preserving, protecting and promoting TK for better socio-economic growth in the country, while also addressing India’s interventions to improve the livelihoods of the indigenous and local communities. Further, the talk covered aspects of Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) and People’s rights, while laying emphasis on ethical practices to be followed to respect the Moral Rights of the concerned knowledge holder(s).</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.pas.va/en/publications/scripta-varia/sv157pas/sattigeri.html"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2025-12-09T10:07:20Z", "timestamp": 1765274840000, "date-parts": [[2025, 12, 9]]}, "isbn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "9788826610146"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "publisher": "Libreria Editrice Vaticana", "reference": [{"DOI": "10.65398/OMJD7446", "key": "ref0", "unstructured": "Alford, H. and von Braun, J. eds., (2025). Indigenous Peoples' Knowledge and the Sciences. Combining Knowledge and Science on Vulnerabilities and Solutions for Resilience. [online] Libreria Editrice Vaticana. Available at: https://www.pas.va/en/publications/scripta-varia/sv157pas.html https://www.doi.org/10.65398/OMJD7446.", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "container-title": ["Indigenous Peoples’ Knowledge and the Sciences: Combining Knowledge and Science on Vulnerabilities and Solutions for Resilience"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "reference-count": 1, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2025]]}, "references-count": 1, "is-referenced-by-count": 0}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The workshop on “Indigenous Peoples’ Knowledge and the Sciences” organised by the Pontifical Academy of Sciences (PAS) and the Pontifical Academy of Social Sciences (PASS) focused on bringing together indigenous knowledge and local communities and the science fraternity to arrive at common understanding, objectives and joint work to address climate change vulnerabilities affecting lives and livelihoods. The workshop witnessed participation from across the world, and India shared its experiences on handling and working with traditional knowledge (TK) and the Traditional Knowledge Digital Library (TKDL). The importance of national government policies was highlighted in the context of preserving, protecting and promoting TK for better socio-economic growth in the country, while also addressing India’s interventions to improve the livelihoods of the indigenous and local communities. Further, the talk covered aspects of Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) and People’s rights, while laying emphasis on ethical practices to be followed to respect the Moral Rights of the concerned knowledge holder(s).</jats:p>", "publisher": "Libreria Editrice Vaticana", "citationCount": 0, "publicationDate": "2025"}, {"id": "cr_10.56042/alis.v72i4.25672", "doi": "10.56042/alis.v72i4.25672", "url": "https://doi.org/10.56042/alis.v72i4.25672", "issn": "0975-2404", "year": 2025, "iss