 the Cyberforest&quot;, basically, how are we to think about the intellectual &quot;commons&quot;, or public domain; and the legitimacy of various types of cultural appropriation. The chapter describes some of the issues in each of these three areas and suggests some tentative connections pointing in the direction of understanding the rapidly emerging politics of intellectual property law, international and otherwise. It talks about the emerging globalized vision of intellectual property protection embedded in multilateral agreements.", "citationCount": 118, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Intellectual property", "Neocolonialism", "Order (exchange)", "Property (philosophy)", "Law and economics"], "publicationDate": "2017-05-15", "publicationType": "book-chapter"}, {"id": "oa_W2300617472", "url": "https://pure.eur.nl/en/publications/5ce47c64-369e-4d84-9d60-17701ffe6750", "year": 2016, "pages": "19", "title": "Bottom of the Data Pyramid: Big Data and the Global South", "venue": "EUR Research Repository (Erasmus University Rotterdam)", "pdfUrl": "https://pure.eur.nl/ws/files/47697913/Bottom-of-the-Data-Pyramid-IJoC-Arora-2016.pdf", "source": "openalex", "volume": "10", "authors": ["Payal Arora"], "rawData": {"id": "https://openalex.org/W2300617472", "doi": null, "ids": {"mag": "2300617472", "openalex": "https://openalex.org/W2300617472"}, "fwci": 16.5733, "mesh": [], "type": "article", "title": "Bottom of the Data Pyramid: Big Data and the Global South", "awards": [], "biblio": {"issue": null, "volume": "10", "last_page": null, "first_page": "19"}, "topics": [{"id": "https://openalex.org/T13194", "field": {"id": "https://openalex.org/fields/17", "display_name": "Computer Science"}, "score": 0.9968000054359436, "domain": {"id": "https://openalex.org/domains/3", "display_name": "Physical Sciences"}, "subfield": {"id": "https://openalex.org/subfields/1710", "display_name": "Information Systems"}, "display_name": "ICT in Developing Communities"}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/T12786", "