ttp://www.ijqr.net/journal/v13-n3/15.pdf"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2019-09-18T09:22:23Z", "timestamp": 1568798543000, "date-parts": [[2019, 9, 18]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "1800-6450"}, {"type": "electronic", "value": "1800-7473"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2019, 9, 15]]}, "publisher": "Faculty of Engineering, University of Kragujevac", "journal-issue": {"issue": "3", "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2019, 9, 18]]}, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 9, 18]]}}, "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "container-title": ["International Journal for Quality Research"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2019, 9, 15]]}, "reference-count": 0, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 9, 15]]}, "references-count": 0, "short-container-title": ["IJQR"], "is-referenced-by-count": 22}, "publisher": "Faculty of Engineering, University of Kragujevac", "citationCount": 22, "publicationDate": "2019-09-15", "journalAbbreviation": "IJQR"}, {"id": "cr_10.35940/ijitee.i8613.0881019", "doi": "10.35940/ijitee.i8613.0881019", "url": "https://doi.org/10.35940/ijitee.i8613.0881019", "issn": "2278-3075", "year": 2019, "issue": "10", "pages": "48-53", "title": "Technological Advancement-Based Paradigm Shift: A Focus Shift from Large Screen to Small Screen", "venue": "International Journal of Innovative Technology and Exploring Engineering", "source": "crossref", "volume": "8", "authors": [",", "Singh, Amandeep", "Singla, Babita", ",", "Jain, Ashu", ","], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.35940/ijitee.i8613.0881019", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.35940/ijitee.i8613.0881019", "ISSN": ["2278-3075"], "link": [{"URL": "https://www.ijitee.org/wp-content/uploads/papers/v8i10/I8613078919.pdf", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "page": "48-53", "type": "journal-article", "issue": "10", "score": 19.655598, "title": ["Technological Advancement-Based Paradigm Shift: A Focus Shift from Large Screen to Small Screen"], "author": [{"name": "Chitkara Business School, Chitkara University, (Punjab), India.", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Amandeep", "family": "Singh", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Babita", "family": "Singla", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"name": "Chitkara Business School, Chitkara University, (Punjab), India.", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Ashu", "family": "Jain", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"name": "Associate Professor. Chitkara Business School, Chitkara University, (Punjab), India.", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2019, 8, 30]]}, "member": "21590", "prefix": "10.35940", "source": "Crossref", "volume": "8", "created": {"date-time": "2019-08-20T09:57:55Z", "timestamp": 1566295075000, "date-parts": [[2019, 8, 20]]}, "indexed": {"date-time": "2024-08-11T05:11:03Z", "timestamp": 1723353063102, "date-parts": [[2024, 8, 11]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Technology has always been behind the paradigm shifts in the business. The businesses have seen their growth by marketing their product through TV, which was considered to be salesman at home that is going to provide all the information. With the advancement in the telecommunication system that has seen a major shift. With the launch of mobile phone things became very easier for business communication. Later with android and iOS introduction everything took by storm. Now most of the viewing is on mobile rather than TV. This research paper highlights the importance of use of mobile based technology to cater the better needs of the consumers. This paper highlights the various upcoming model to cater the market based on the upcoming technologies. This paper shows how the technology is helping the companies in attracting the customers.</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ijitee.org/portfolio-item/I8613078919/"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2022-09-28T08:46:24Z", "timestamp": 1664354784000, "date-parts": [[2022, 9, 28]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "electronic", "value": "2278-3075"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2019, 8, 30]]}, "publisher": "Blue Eyes Intelligence Engineering and Sciences Engineering and Sciences Publication - BEIESP", "journal-issue": {"issue": "10", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 8, 30]]}}, "update-policy": "http://dx.doi.org/10.35940/beiesp.crossmarkpolicy", "content-domain": {"domain": ["www.ijitee.org"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "container-title": ["International Journal of Innovative Technology and Exploring Engineering"], "reference-count": 0, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 8, 30]]}, "references-count": 0, "short-container-title": ["IJITEE"], "is-referenced-by-count": 15}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Technology has always been behind the paradigm shifts in the business. The businesses have seen their growth by marketing their product through TV, which was considered to be salesman at home that is going to provide all the information. With the advancement in the telecommunication system that has seen a major shift. With the launch of mobile phone things became very easier for business communication. Later with android and iOS introduction everything took by storm. Now most of the viewing is on mobile rather than TV. This research paper highlights the importance of use of mobile based technology to cater the better needs of the consumers. This paper highlights the various upcoming model to cater the market based on the upcoming technologies. This paper shows how the technology is helping the companies in attracting the customers.</jats:p>", "publisher": "Blue Eyes Intelligence Engineering and Sciences Engineering and Sciences Publication - BEIESP", "citationCount": 15, "publicationDate": "2019-08-30", "journalAbbreviation": "IJITEE"}, {"id": "cr_10.35940/ijrte.e5841.018520", "doi": "10.35940/ijrte.e5841.018520", "url": "https://doi.org/10.35940/ijrte.e5841.018520", "issn": "2277-3878", "year": 2020, "issue": "5", "pages": "2296-2300", "title": "Impact of E-Banking Service Quality on Customer Satisfaction", "venue": "International Journal of Recent Technology and Engineering (IJRTE)", "source": "crossref", "volume": "8", "authors": [",", "Sharma*, Jyotsna", "Singh, Jagdeep", ",", "Singh, Amandeep", ","], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.35940/ijrte.e5841.018520", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.35940/ijrte.e5841.018520", "ISSN": ["2277-3878"], "link": [{"URL": "https://www.ijrte.org/wp-content/uploads/papers/v8i5/E5841018520.pdf", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "page": "2296-2300", "type": "journal-article", "issue": "5", "score": 18.908684, "title": ["Impact of E-Banking Service Quality on Customer Satisfaction"], "author": [{"name": "Faculty of Management, Asian Educational Institute, Punjab, India", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Jyotsna", "family": "Sharma*", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Jagdeep", "family": "Singh", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"name": "Dean, GNA Business School, GNA University Punjab India.", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Amandeep", "family": "Singh", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"name": "Chitkara Business School, Chitkara University, Punjab, India.", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2020, 1, 30]]}, "member": "21590", "prefix": "10.35940", "source": "Crossref", "volume": "8", "created": {"date-time": "2020-02-11T04:36:40Z", "timestamp": 1581395800000, "date-parts": [[2020, 2, 11]]}, "indexed": {"date-time": "2025-10-26T22:54:54Z", "timestamp": 1761519294525, "date-parts": [[2025, 10, 26]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The main objective of this paper is to measure the impact of E-banking service quality on customer satisfaction. Primary data method is used to collect data by using the interview method over 504 respondents. The random sampling technique has been taken up for the survey by keeping due care for the availability and easiness of the customers. The Multiple regression technique has been employed to measure the effect to service quality dimension on the customer satisfaction. The paper examines the relative strength of each dimension affecting customer satisfaction. It has been found that the overall regression model has been a reasonable fit and there is a statistically significant association between service quality dimension and customer satisfaction.</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ijrte.org/portfolio-item/E5841018520/"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2022-04-25T07:42:52Z", "timestamp": 1650872572000, "date-parts": [[2022, 4, 25]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "electronic", "value": "2277-3878"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2020, 1, 30]]}, "publisher": "Blue Eyes Intelligence Engineering and Sciences Engineering and Sciences Publication - BEIESP", "journal-issue": {"issue": "5", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2020, 1, 30]]}}, "update-policy": "http://dx.doi.org/10.35940/beiesp.crossmarkpolicy", "content-domain": {"domain": ["www.ijrte.org"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "container-title": ["International Journal of Recent Technology and Engineering (IJRTE)"], "reference-count": 0, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2020, 1, 30]]}, "references-count": 0, "short-container-title": ["IJRTE"], "is-referenced-by-count": 9}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The main objective of this paper is to measure the impact of E-banking service quality on customer satisfaction. Primary data method is used to collect data by using the interview method over 504 respondents. The random sampling technique has been taken up for the survey by keeping due care for the availability and easiness of the customers. The Multiple regression technique has been employed to measure the effect to service quality dimension on the customer satisfaction. The paper examines the relative strength of each dimension affecting customer satisfaction. It has been found that the overall regression model has been a reasonable fit and there is a statistically significant association between service quality dimension and customer satisfaction.</jats:p>", "publisher": "Blue Eyes Intelligence Engineering and Sciences Engineering and Sciences Publication - BEIESP", "citationCount": 9, "publicationDate": "2020-01-30", "journalAbbreviation": "IJRTE"}, {"id": "cr_10.5295/cdg.201320ak", "doi": "10.5295/cdg.201320ak", "url": "https://doi.org/10.5295/cdg.201320ak", "issn": "1131-6837", "year": 2021, "pages": "49-62", "title": "An Empirical Analysis of the Factors Influencing Social Entrepreneurship: A Gendered Approach", "venue": "Cuadernos de Gestión", "source": "crossref", "authors": [",", "Khursheed, Ambreen", "Fatima, Maham", ",", "Mustafa, Dr. Faisal", ",", "Nawaz Lodhi, Dr. Rab", ",", "Akhtar, Ayesha", ","], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.5295/cdg.201320ak", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.5295/cdg.201320ak", "ISSN": ["1131-6837", "1988-2157"], "page": "49-62", "type": "journal-article", "score": 20.046347, "title": ["An Empirical Analysis of the Factors Influencing Social Entrepreneurship: A Gendered Approach"], "author": [{"name": "Senior Lecturer, PhD Scholar, UCP Business School, University of Central Punjab, Pakistan –ambreen.khursheed@ucp.edu.pk", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1497-5848", "given": "Ambreen", "family": "Khursheed", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8407-6162", "given": "Maham", "family": "Fatima", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}, {"name": "Research Associate, UCP Business School, University of Central Punjab, Pakistan –maham.fatima@ucp.edu.pk", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4689-5711", "given": "Dr. Faisal", "family": "Mustafa", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}, {"name": "Professor, Dean UCP Business School, University of Central Punjab, Pakistan– faisal.mustafa@ucp.edu.pk", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2120-358X", "given": "Dr. Rab", "family": "Nawaz Lodhi", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}, {"name": "Associate Professor, UCP Business School, University of Central Punjab, Pakistan– rabnawaz.lodhi@ucp.edu.pk", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8373-5958", "given": "Ayesha", "family": "Akhtar", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}, {"name": "Research Associate, UCP Business School, University of Central Punjab, Pakistan– ayeshaakhtar@ucp.edu.pk", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2021, 11, 1]]}, "member": "3251", "prefix": "10.5295", "source": "Crossref", "created": {"date-time": "2021-03-01T07:42:02Z", "timestamp": 1614584522000, "date-parts": [[2021, 3, 1]]}, "indexed": {"version": "3.40.5", "date-time": "2026-01-02T07:24:53Z", "timestamp": 1767338693663, "date-parts": [[2026, 1, 2]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Purpose: This study examines how entrepreneurial ecosystem factors (entrepreneurial finance, entrepreneurial education, physical and commercial infrastructure, culture, and R&amp;D transfer activities) shape social entrepreneurial activities (SEA) of men and women. Design/methodology/approach: Panel data from 35 countries are examined through General Methods of Moments (GMM) with Arellano Bond tests for the period of ten years (2005-2014). Findings: Our results indicate that women are more likely to get involved in creation of social ventures. Further, the selected six entrepreneurial factors modify SEA in a significantly different manner for both genders. Originality/value: Based on this analysis, this study is the first to provide deeper insights for improving the assessment of social entrepreneurial activities in efficiency and innovation driven economies within the entrepreneurial ecosystem.</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://ojs.ehu.eus/index.php/CG/article/view/22641"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2023-11-23T07:52:10Z", "timestamp": 1700725930000, "date-parts": [[2023, 11, 23]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "1131-6837"}, {"type": "electronic", "value": "1988-2157"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2021, 11, 1]]}, "publisher": "Enpresa Institutua - Instituto de Economia Aplicada a la Empresa", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "container-title": ["Cuadernos de Gestión"], "reference-count": 0, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2021, 11, 1]]}, "references-count": 0, "short-container-title": ["cuadernosgestion"], "is-referenced-by-count": 8}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Purpose: This study examines how entrepreneurial ecosystem factors (entrepreneurial finance, entrepreneurial education, physical and commercial infrastructure, culture, and R&amp;D transfer activities) shape social entrepreneurial activities (SEA) of men and women. Design/methodology/approach: Panel data from 35 countries are examined through General Methods of Moments (GMM) with Arellano Bond tests for the period of ten years (2005-2014). Findings: Our results indicate that women are more likely to get involved in creation of social ventures. Further, the selected six entrepreneurial factors modify SEA in a significantly different manner for both genders. Originality/value: Based on this analysis, this study is the first to provide deeper insights for improving the assessment of social entrepreneurial activities in efficiency and innovation driven economies within the entrepreneurial ecosystem.</jats:p>", "publisher": "Enpresa Institutua - Instituto de Economia Aplicada a la Empresa", "citationCount": 8, "publicationDate": "2021-11-01", "journalAbbreviation": "cuadernosgestion"}, {"id": "cr_10.35940/ijitee.l3281.1081219", "doi": "10.35940/ijitee.l3281.1081219", "url": "https://doi.org/10.35940/ijitee.l3281.1081219", "issn": "2278-3075", "year": 2019, "issue": "12", "pages": "367-370", "title": "Contract Manufacturing: The Boon for Developing Economies", "venue": "International Journal of Innovative Technology and Exploring Engineering", "source": "crossref", "volume": "8", "authors": [",", "Singla*, Babita", "Singh, Amandeep", ","], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.35940/ijitee.l3281.1081219", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.35940/ijitee.l3281.1081219", "ISSN": ["2278-3075"], "link": [{"URL": "https://www.ijitee.org/wp-content/uploads/papers/v8i12/L32811081219.pdf", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "page": "367-370", "type": "journal-article", "issue": "12", "score": 18.62978, "title": ["Contract Manufacturing: The Boon for Developing Economies"], "author": [{"name": "Chitkara Business School, Chitkara University, Punjab, India", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Babita", "family": "Singla*", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Amandeep", "family": "Singh", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"name": "Chitkara Business School, Chitkara University, Punjab, India", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 30]]}, "member": "21590", "prefix": "10.35940", "source": "Crossref", "volume": "8", "created": {"date-time": "2019-10-22T03:25:24Z", "timestamp": 1571714724000, "date-parts": [[2019, 10, 22]]}, "indexed": {"date-time": "2025-11-11T15:48:40Z", "timestamp": 1762876120935, "date-parts": [[2025, 11, 11]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The paper highlights about the Business to Business Scenario in India mainly in terms of the status of contract manufacturing approach. This work also tries to find the role &amp; importance of contract manufacturers in the Indian Industry. The impact of various factors like regulatory pressure, industry competition, change in patent regime &amp; labour cost arbitrage is also looked upon. The paper highlights the need for contract manufacturing in this particular sector for domestic &amp; international sales. The paper concludes by emphasizing on the fact that the industry is in growth stage and if it is able to integrate various growth factors, it’ll be one of the most promising sectors in India.</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ijitee.org/portfolio-item/L32811081219/"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2022-07-26T07:26:49Z", "timestamp": 1658820409000, "date-parts": [[2022, 7, 26]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "electronic", "value": "2278-3075"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 30]]}, "publisher": "Blue Eyes Intelligence Engineering and Sciences Engineering and Sciences Publication - BEIESP", "journal-issue": {"issue": "12", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 30]]}}, "update-policy": "http://dx.doi.org/10.35940/beiesp.crossmarkpolicy", "content-domain": {"domain": ["www.ijitee.org"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "container-title": ["International Journal of Innovative Technology and Exploring Engineering"], "reference-count": 0, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 30]]}, "references-count": 0, "short-container-title": ["IJITEE"], "is-referenced-by-count": 4}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The paper highlights about the Business to Business Scenario in India mainly in terms of the status of contract manufacturing approach. This work also tries to find the role &amp; importance of contract manufacturers in the Indian Industry. The impact of various factors like regulatory pressure, industry competition, change in patent regime &amp; labour cost arbitrage is also looked upon. The paper highlights the need for contract manufacturing in this particular sector for domestic &amp; international sales. The paper concludes by emphasizing on the fact that the industry is in growth stage and if it is able to integrate various growth factors, it’ll be one of the most promising sectors in India.</jats:p>", "publisher": "Blue Eyes Intelligence Engineering and Sciences Engineering and Sciences Publication - BEIESP", "citationCount": 4, "publicationDate": "2019-10-30", "journalAbbreviation": "IJITEE"}, {"id": "cr_10.15415/jtmge.2019.102007", "doi": "10.15415/jtmge.2019.102007", "url": "https://doi.org/10.15415/jtmge.2019.102007", "issn": "0976-545X", "year": 2019, "issue": "2", "pages": "82-88", "title": "Investment Attitude of Working Women: A Study of Education Sector in Punjab", "venue": "Journal of Technology Management for Growing Economies", "pdfUrl": "https://tmg.chitkara.edu.in/index.php/tmge/article/download/149/97", "source": "crossref", "volume": "10", "authors": [",", "Sharma, Poonam", "Kaur, Navdeep", ","], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.15415/jtmge.2019.102007", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.15415/jtmge.2019.102007", "ISSN": ["0976-545X", "2456-3226"], "link": [{"URL": "https://tmg.chitkara.edu.in/index.php/tmge/article/download/149/97", "content-type": "application/pdf", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "text-mining"}, {"URL": "https://tmg.chitkara.edu.in/index.php/tmge/article/download/149/97", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "page": "82-88", "type": "journal-article", "issue": "2", "score": 18.629837, "title": ["Investment Attitude of Working Women: A Study of Education Sector in Punjab"], "author": [{"name": "P.G. Department of Commerce & Business Administration, Khalsa College Amritsar -143005, Punjab, India", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Poonam", "family": "Sharma", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Navdeep", "family": "Kaur", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"name": "P.G. Department of Commerce & Business Administration, Khalsa College Amritsar -143005, Punjab, India", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 25]]}, "member": "6090", "prefix": "10.15415", "source": "Crossref", "volume": "10", "created": {"date-time": "2020-06-25T09:24:59Z", "timestamp": 1593077099000, "date-parts": [[2020, 6, 25]]}, "indexed": {"date-time": "2024-08-06T14:58:32Z", "timestamp": 1722956312947, "date-parts": [[2024, 8, 6]]}, "license": [{"URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0", "start": {"date-time": "2019-10-25T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1571961600000, "date-parts": [[2019, 10, 25]]}, "delay-in-days": 0, "content-version": "unspecified"}], "abstract": "<jats:p>Investment is important for improving productivity and increasing the competitiveness of an economy. The present paper is an attempt to explore the factors influencing the investment attitude of women working in the education sector in the Punjab State in India. Even though, general profile of women investors is changing in tune with time, but they are insulating in various spheres of investment such as awareness and preference of investment. Today, the role of women has changed from “Savers to Investors”. Factor Analytical results revealed that women investors prefer to invest in risk free securities. The level of financial knowledge also influences their investment attitude. The present study reveals the factors namely; secure investment avenues, financial literacy, stock market investment and post office schemes, bank deposits, physical assets, risk taking ability and concern for financial matters that are important to women working in education sector.</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://tmg.chitkara.edu.in/2019/investment-attitude-of-working-women-a-study-of-education-sector-in-punjab/"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2024-05-31T06:44:01Z", "timestamp": 1717137841000, "date-parts": [[2024, 5, 31]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "0976-545X"}, {"type": "electronic", "value": "2456-3226"}], "published": {"date