online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 10, 25]]}, "references-count": 15, "short-container-title": ["JTMGE"], "is-referenced-by-count": 2}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Investment is important for improving productivity and increasing the competitiveness of an economy. The present paper is an attempt to explore the factors influencing the investment attitude of women working in the education sector in the Punjab State in India. Even though, general profile of women investors is changing in tune with time, but they are insulating in various spheres of investment such as awareness and preference of investment. Today, the role of women has changed from “Savers to Investors”. Factor Analytical results revealed that women investors prefer to invest in risk free securities. The level of financial knowledge also influences their investment attitude. The present study reveals the factors namely; secure investment avenues, financial literacy, stock market investment and post office schemes, bank deposits, physical assets, risk taking ability and concern for financial matters that are important to women working in education sector.</jats:p>", "publisher": "Chitkara University Publications", "citationCount": 2, "publicationDate": "2019-10-25", "journalAbbreviation": "JTMGE"}, {"id": "cr_10.53908/nmmr.300104", "doi": "10.53908/nmmr.300104", "url": "https://doi.org/10.53908/nmmr.300104", "issn": "0971-1023", "year": 2022, "issue": "01", "pages": "68-89", "title": "Exploring the link between Innovativeness and Organizational Performance", "venue": "NMIMS Management Review", "source": "crossref", "volume": "30", "authors": [",", "Thakur, Pratibha", "Saxena, Charu", ",", "Arora, Rupali", ","], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.53908/nmmr.300104", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.53908/nmmr.300104", "ISSN": ["0971-1023"], "page": "68-89", "type": "journal-article", "issue": "01", "score": 18.608322, "title": ["Exploring the link between Innovativeness and Organizational Performance"], "author": [{"name": "Assistant Professor at Chandigarh Group of Colleges, Landran, Kharar Banur Highway, Punjab", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6386-3960", "given": "Pratibha", "family": "Thakur", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1500-8772", "given": "Charu", "family": "Saxena", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}, {"name": "Assistant Professor, University School of Business, Chandigarh University, Mohali, Punjab", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0783-3916", "given": "Rupali", "family": "Arora", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "authenticated-orcid": false}, {"name": "Professor, University School of Business, Chandigarh University, Mohali, Punjab", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": []}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2022, 3, 25]]}, "member": "179", "prefix": "10.1177", "source": "Crossref", "volume": "30", "created": {"date-time": "2022-04-05T09:40:04Z", "timestamp": 1649151604000, "date-parts": [[2022, 4, 5]]}, "indexed": {"version": "3.40.5", "date-time": "2025-05-14T13:28:08Z", "timestamp": 1747229288439, "date-parts": [[2025, 5, 14]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Purpose: The present paper is an attempt to examine the impact of innovativeness on organizational performance. The investigation was carried out in Information Technology (IT) industry of Northern region of India.  Methodology: A sample of 420 employees working in the Northern region was analyzed by applying Partial Least Square Structural Equation Modeling 3.0 (PLSSEM) and Statistical Package for Social Sciences (SPSS).  Findings: The key objective of the present research is to identify the dimensions of organizational innovativeness that has an effect on organizational performance. The findings revealed that product, process and marketing innovativeness have a significant and positive impact on organizational performance, whereas, the impact of behavioral innovativeness on performance is not significant.  Practical Implications: The outcomes of the study provide important insights to the policy makers and strategists to redesign the innovation practices and strategies that will further help in improving organizational performance.  Originality: Limited studies have been conducted in IT sector of Northern region in order to determine the role of innovativness in predicting organizational performance. Therefore, the results of this study contributes to the existing literature and also presents the perception of employees regarding the role of innovation to improve organizational performance.</jats:p>", "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://management-review.nmims.edu/2022/03/exploring-the-link-between-innovativeness-andorganizational-performance/"}}, "deposited": {"date-time": "2024-07-08T13:18:05Z", "timestamp": 1720444685000, "date-parts": [[2024, 7, 8]]}, "issn-type": [{"type": "print", "value": "0971-1023"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2022, 3, 25]]}, "publisher": "SAGE Publications", "journal-issue": {"issue": "01", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2022, 3, 25]]}}, "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "container-title": ["NMIMS Management Review"], "reference-count": 0, "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2022, 3, 25]]}, "references-count": 0, "short-container-title": ["NMMR"], "is-referenced-by-count": 2}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Purpose: The present paper is an attempt to examine the impact of innovativeness on organizational performance. The investigation was carried out in Information Technology (IT) industry of Northern region of India.  Methodology: A sample of 420 employees working in the Northern region was analyzed by applying Partial Least Square Structural Equation Modeling 3.0 (PLSSEM) and Statistical Package for Social Sciences (SPSS).  Findings: The key objective of the present research is to identify the dimensions of organizational innovativeness that has an effect on organizational performance. The findings revealed that product, process and marketing innovativeness have a significant and positive impact on organizational performance, whereas, the impact of behavioral innovativeness on performance is not significant.  Practical Implications: The outcomes of the study provide important insights to the policy makers and strategists to redesign the innovation practices and strategies that will further help in improving organizational performance.  Originality: Limited studies have been conducted in IT sector of Northern region in order to determine the role of innovativness in predicting organizational performance. Therefore, the results of this study contributes to the existing literature and also presents the perception of employees regarding the role of innovation to improve organizational performance.</jats:p>", "publisher": "SAGE Publications", "citationCount": 2, "publicationDate": "2022-03-25", "journalAbbreviation": "NMMR"}, {"id": "cr_10.9790/487x-16234757", "doi": "10.9790/487x-16234757", "url": "https://doi.org/10.9790/487x-16234757", "issn": "2319-7668", "year": 2014, "issue": "2", "pages": "47-57", "title": "Consumer Behavior of Purchase of Processed Cereal Food Products in Punjab", "venue": "IOSR Journal of Business and Management", "source": "crossref", "volume": "16", "authors": [",", "Kaur, Inderpreet", "Singh, Sukhdev"], "rawData": {"DOI": "10.9790/487x-16234757", "URL": "https://doi.org/10.9790/487x-16234757", "ISSN": ["2319-7668", "2278-487X"], "page": "47-57", "type": "journal-article", "issue": "2", "score": 19.186222, "title": ["Consumer Behavior of Purchase of Processed Cereal Food Products in Punjab"], "author": [{"name": "Assistant Professor, Department of Business Administration, Guru Nanak Institute of Management and Technology, Ludhiana, Punjab Technical University,Punjab, India", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": []}, {"given": "Inderpreet",