: [96], "unsupervised": [94, 136], "pre-training.": [171], "document-level": [134], "initialization": [107], "modifications.": [101], "reconstructing": [72], "sentence-level": [90], "document-level)": [92], "highest-resource": [115], "sequence-to-sequence": [23, 52]}, "cited_by_percentile_year": {"max": 100, "min": 90}, "corresponding_author_ids": ["https://openalex.org/A5004412943", "https://openalex.org/A5011974509", "https://openalex.org/A5016113002", "https://openalex.org/A5019081674", "https://openalex.org/A5061256224", "https://openalex.org/A5067919401", "https://openalex.org/A5075834790", "https://openalex.org/A5112542984"], "countries_distinct_count": 2, "institutions_distinct_count": 8, "corresponding_institution_ids": ["https://openalex.org/I2252078561", "https://openalex.org/I4210114444"], "sustainable_development_goals": [{"id": "https://metadata.un.org/sdg/4", "score": 0.5699999928474426, "display_name": "Quality Education"}], "citation_normalized_percentile": {"value": 0.9995073, "is_in_top_1_percent": true, "is_in_top_10_percent": true}}, "abstract": "This paper demonstrates that multilingual denoising pre-training produces significant performance gains across a wide variety of machine translation (MT) tasks. We present mBART—a sequence-to-sequence denoising auto-encoder pre-trained on large-scale monolingual corpora in many languages using the BART objective (Lewis et al., 2019 ). mBART is the first method for pre-training a complete sequence-to-sequence model by denoising full texts in multiple languages, whereas previous approaches have focused only on the encoder, decoder, or reconstructing parts of the text. Pre-training a complete model allows it to be directly fine-tuned for supervised (both sentence-level and document-level) and unsupervised machine translation, with no task- specific modifications. We demonstrate that adding mBART initialization produces performance gains in all but the highest-resource settings, including up to 12 BLEU points for low resource MT and over 5 BLEU points for many document-level and unsupervised models. We also show that it enables transfer to language pairs with no bi-text or that were not in the pre-training corpus, and present extensive analysis of which factors contribute the most to effective pre-training. 1", "publisher": "Association for Computational Linguistics", "citationCount": 994, "fieldsOfStudy": ["Computer science", "Machine translation", "Initialization", "Artificial intelligence", "Encoder"], "publicationDate": "2020-11-25", "publicationType": "journal-article", "journalAbbreviation": "Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics"}, {"id": "oa_W3107826490", "doi": "10.48550/arxiv.2001.08210", "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2001.08210", "year": 2020, "title": "Multilingual Denoising Pre-training for Neural Machine Translation", "venue": "arXiv (Cornell University)", "pdfUrl": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.08210", "source": "openalex", "authors": ["Yinhan Liu", "Jiatao Gu", "Naman Goyal", "Xian Li", "Sergey Edunov", "Marjan Ghazvininejad", "Mike Lewis", "Luke Zettlemoyer"], "rawData": {"id": "https://openalex.org/W3107826490", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2001.08210", "ids": {"doi": "https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2001.08210", "mag": "3107826490", "openalex": "https://openalex.org/W3107826490"}, "fwci": null, "mesh": [], "type": "preprint", "title": "Multilingual Denoising Pre-training for Neural Machine Translation", "awards": [], "biblio": {"issue": null, "volume": null, "last_page": null, "first_page": null}, "topics": [{"id": "https://openalex.org/T10181", "field": {"id": "https://openalex.org/fields/17", "display_name": "Computer Science"}, "score": 1, "domain": {"id": "https://openalex.org/domains/3", "display_name": "Physical Sciences"}, "subfield": {"id": "https://openalex.org/subfields/1702", "display_name": "Artificial Intelligence"}, "display_name": "Natural Language Processing Techniques"}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/T100