ing systems, is sourced directly from in-house adaptive R&D conducted at Lovely Professional University (LPU) . This approach ensures that the technologies are context-appropriate, addressing the specific needs and constraints of the Phulkari artisan community in Jalandhar. LPU’s established expertise in developing and validating technologies for rural and MSME sectors  underpins the credibility of this source. The adaptive R&D process inherently involves iterative design and testing within comparable settings, mitigating the risk of a top-down R&D disconnect often seen in technology transfer models . This in-house approach allows for the fine-tuning of technologies like ergonomic winders and temperature-controlled dye baths to preserve the traditional Phulkari aesthetic patterns while enhancing productivity and reducing occupational hazards. The validation of these technologies through participatory action research (PAR) and community-managed demonstration units within the Jalandhar micro-clusters further solidifies their feasibility and suitability for widespread adoption by 2,000 artisans.	259	DRAFT	f	5	2026-04-28 06:10:06.465	2026-04-28 12:06:16.289	2026-04-28 12:06:16.286	single_pass	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"grantDraftReadiness": {"issues": [], "warnings": []}, "grantComplianceReport": {"stage": "pass2", "passed": false, "generatedAt": "2026-04-28T12:06:16.268Z", "hardFailures": [{"key": "template_required_fact_1", "source": "template", "message": "Required grant constraint is missing: Template required fact 1", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Source of identified Technology/ package of practice under project\\"."}, {"key": "required_directly answer source o", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required point is still missing: Directly answer \\"Source of identified Technology/ package of practice under project\\".", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Source of identified Technology/ package of practice under project\\"."}, {"key": "required_validation evidenc