cmoi88gg700g440wtozhrn0aw	cmodzbetg008nxrslnjerg39y	proposed_objectives	proposed_objectives	This proposal aims to achieve the following core objectives: 1) Design and validate context-appropriate, semi-mechanized yarn preparation tools and eco-friendly, temperature-controlled dye baths specifically for the Phulkari craft. 2) Establish a centralized STI Hub in Jalandhar to serve as a nexus for technology adoption, training, and knowledge dissemination for 2,000 marginalized women artisans. 3) Enhance the socio-economic empowerment of these artisans by increasing their average monthly income by 50% and fostering generational preservation of the Phulkari heritage through S&T interventions. 4) Develop a scalable and sustainable model for technology transfer and artisan governance within MSME micro-clusters, aligning with national initiatives like SFURTI. Success will be recognized through the quantifiable adoption of new technologies, demonstrable income increases, the successful operation of the Hub, and the documented preservation of Indigenous Knowledge Systems (IKS) related to the craft.	135	\N	\N	TASK: GRANT SECTION DRAFT - PROPOSED OBJECTIVES\n\nYou are writing a grant proposal section for reviewers inside Grapsi.\nWrite reviewer-facing proposal prose, not a journal manuscript section.\n\nGRANT CONTEXT:\n- Project: Grant: STI Hubs\n- Funding call: STI Hubs\n- Agency: Department of Science and Technology\n- Prep keywords: 2,000 artisans, Technology adoption, Generational preservation, Phulkari craft, MSME clusters, Scale\n\nSEEDED CONTEXT:\n- Treat this frozen workspace context as grounding. Reuse it where relevant; do not contradict it.\n- Project: Grant: STI Hubs\n- Funding call: STI Hubs\n- Agency: Department of Science and Technology\n- Deadline: 2026-05-16\n- Project duration: 3 years\n- Eligibility: The following organizations/institutes are eligible for receiving financial support for establishment of STI Hubs. Government Academic Institutions (Central and S