Technology gap, Context - appropriate tools, Ergonomic, Semi - mechanized yarn winders, Temperature - controlled, Eco - friendly dye baths, Eco - friendly processing, Increase average monthly income, 50%, MSME cooperative, Post - grant, Phulkari preservation model, Cooperative model, Master trainers, Usage fee, Buy - back agreements, MSME cooperative model, Scalable blueprint, State backing, Regional textile clusters\n\nEVIDENCE DIGEST (one line per citation - use as grounding, not verbatim):\n\n- [Shafi2022] [MUST-CITE]: BACKGROUND | Provides a systematic review of innovation in traditional handicraft companies, linking innovation to sustainable development and competitiveness. | strength: weak | stance: neutral | role: show gap | method: Systematic literature review with keyword-based search and analysis. | use: Use this citation to name the limitation, barrier, or unmet need.\n\nEVIDENCE GAPS:\nDesign and impact of semi-mechanized yarn winders and dye baths for artisan use, Role of STI Hubs in enhancing livelihoods for women artisans in MSME clusters, Community-based technology adoption models via Self-Help Groups (SHGs)\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n- Return ONLY clean Markdown. No JSON, no code fences, no preamble.\n- Preserve [CITE:key] anchors exactly when mapped evidence is used.\n- Default to a single compact block unless the template clearly requires bullets.	This proposal establishes a Science, Technology, and Innovation (STI) Hub to address critical livelihood challenges for 2,000 marginalized women Phulkari artisans in Jalandhar, Punjab. The current manual production methods create significant output restrictions and low wages (under ₹5,000/month), leading to artisans abandoning the craft. Our S&T intervention, sourced from in-house adaptive R&D, introduces context-appropriate, semi-mechanized tools like ergonomic winders and eco-friendly dye baths, designed to boost production by 50% and double wages without compromising traditional aesthetics. Technology adoption and artisan mobilization are facilitated through existing Self-Help Groups (SHGs), ensuring immediate trust and effective uptake, with SHG leaders actively participating in the Hub Steering Committee for genuine artisan governance. This project directly synergizes with the MSME SFURTI scheme to augment existing textile micro-clusters, aligning with DST priorities for socio-economic development and generational preservation of the Phulkari craft. The expected payoff is enhanced livelihoods, capacity building, and a scalable blueprint for community-managed technology adoption in MSME clusters, contributing to sustainable development.	233	DRAFT	f	9	2026-04-28 06:10:00.356	2026-04-28 12:03:40.697	2026-04-28 12:03:40.692	single_pass	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"grantDraftReadiness": {"issues": [], "warnings": []}, "grantComplianceReport": {"stage": "pass2", "passed": false, "generatedAt": "2026-04-28T12:03:40.677Z", "hardFailures": [{"key": "template_required_fact_1", "source": "template", "message": "Required grant constraint is missing: Template required fact 1", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Project Summary\\"."}, {"key": "required_directly answer project ", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required point is still missing: Directly answer \\"Project Summary\\".", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Project Summary\\"."}, {"key": "required_scale burden or urgency ", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required point is still missing: Scale, burden, or urgency of including livelihood of proposed area", "ruleText": "Scale, burden, or urgency of including livelihood of proposed area"}, {"key": "evidence_directly answer project ", "source": "template", "message": "Required drafting evidence is missing: Directly answer \\"Project Summary\\".", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Project Summary\\"."}], "softWarnings": [{"key": "reviewer_signal_1", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required grant constraint is missing: Reviewer signal 1", "ruleText": "including livelihood of p