cmoi88a5900du40wtadvf6al4	cmodzbetg008nxrslnjerg39y	background_of_target_community	background_of_target_community	The target community comprises approximately 2,000 Phulkari artisan women in the Jalandhar region of Punjab. These women, predominantly from Scheduled Caste (SC) and Other Backward Classes (OBC) communities (70% of the total), alongside 20% General and 10% Economically Weaker Sections (EWS), possess deep-rooted Indigenous Knowledge (IK) and skills in Phulkari embroidery, a craft integral to their cultural heritage. However, their current livelihood conditions are precarious, with average monthly incomes falling below ₹5,000. This low income, stemming from manual, labor-intensive processes in yarn preparation and dyeing that restrict output and productivity, forces many artisans to abandon the craft in search of more sustainable livelihoods, threatening generational preservation. Existing responses, such as broader MSME initiatives, often fail to address the specific technological bottlenecks and ergonomic challenges faced by these micro-cluster artisans, leading to a technology gap and a disconnect between traditional aesthetics and the demands of modern markets. This proposal is justified now to address this urgent need by introducing context-appropriate, semi-mechanized tools and eco-friendly processing methods, thereby enhancing productivity, increasing incomes, and ensuring the continuity of the Phulkari heritage. [CITE:Mamidipudi2016] [CITE:Shrivastava2020]	180	\N	\N	TASK: GRANT SECTION DRAFT - BACKGROUND OF TARGET COMMUNITY\n\nYou are writing a grant proposal section for reviewers inside Grapsi.\nWrite reviewer-facing proposal prose, not a journal manuscript section.\n\nGRANT CONTEXT:\n- Project: Grant: STI Hubs\n- Funding call: STI Hubs\n- Agency: Department of Science and Technology\n- Prep keywords: 2,000 artisans, Technology adoption, Generational preservation, Phulkari craft, MSME clusters, Scale\n\nSEEDED CONTEXT:\n- Treat this frozen workspa