T (one line per citation - use as grounding, not verbatim):\n\n- [Mamidipudi2016] [MUST-CITE]: BACKGROUND | Establishes a theoretical framework for innovation in handloom weaving, grounded in the socio-economic reality of 4.33 million craftspeople. | strength: medium | stance: neutral | role: prove burden | use: Attach this citation to the exact burden statistic or urgency fact.\n- [Shrivastava2020]: BACKGROUND | Reviews sustainable approaches to rejuvenate handloom and handicraft sectors, emphasizing their role in rural economy and cultural heritage. | strength: medium | stance: neutral | role: show gap | method: Research study (likely literature review or survey) on current state and sustain | use: Use this citation to name the limitation, barrier, or unmet need.\n\nEVIDENCE GAPS:\nLivelihood analysis and income levels of Phulkari artisans in the Jalandhar region, Intersection of traditional skills and modern technology for artisan empowerment\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n- Return ONLY clean Markdown. No JSON, no code fences, no preamble.\n- Preserve [CITE:key] anchors exactly when mapped evidence is used.\n- Default to a single compact block unless the template clearly requires bullets.	The target community comprises approximately 2,000 Phulkari artisan women in the Jalandhar region of Punjab. These women, predominantly from Scheduled Caste (SC) and Other Backward Classes (OBC) communities (70% of the total), alongside 20% General and 10% Economically Weaker Sections (EWS), possess deep-rooted Indigenous Knowledge (IK) and skills in Phulkari embroidery, a craft integral to their cultural heritage. However, their current livelihood conditions are precarious, with average monthly incomes falling below ₹5,000. This low income, stemming from manual, labor-intensive processes in yarn preparation and dyeing that restrict output and productivity, forces many artisans to abandon the craft in search of more sustainable livelihoods, threatening generational preservation. Existing responses, such as broader MSME initiatives, often fail to address the specific technological bottlenecks and ergonomic challenges faced by these micro-cluster artisans, leading to a technology gap and a disconnect between traditional aesthetics and the demands of modern markets. This proposal is justified now to address this urgent need by introducing context-appropriate, semi-mechanized tools and eco-friendly processing methods, thereby enhancing productivity, increasing incomes, and ensuring the continuity of the Phulkari heritage. [CITE:Mamidipudi2016] [CITE:Shrivastava2020]	277	DRAFT	f	6	2026-04-28 06:10:00.669	2026-04-28 12:04:01.374	2026-04-28 12:04:01.37	single_pass	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"grantDraftReadiness": {"issues": [], "warnings": []}, "grantComplianceReport": {"stage": "pass2", "passed": false, "generatedAt": "2026-04-28T12:04:01.353Z", "hardFailures": [{"key": "template_required_fact_1", "source": "template", "message": "Required grant constraint is missing: Template required fact 1", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Background of target community\\"."}, {"key": "required_directly answer backgrou", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required point is still missing: Directly answer \\"Background of target community\\".", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Background of target community\\"."}, {"key": "required_scale burden or urgency ", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required point is still missing: Scale, burden, or urgency of demographic details of target population including their present livelihood conditions", "ruleText": "Scale, burden, or urgency of demographic details of target population including their present livelihood conditions"}, {"key": "required_limitations of current r", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required point is still missing: Limitations of current responses for Present average income level is under ₹5,000/month", "ruleText": "Limitations of current responses for Present average income level is under ₹5,000/month"}, {