rant: STI Hubs\nResearch Question: How should the proposal satisfy PART 3: PROBLEM IDENTIFICATION AND PROPOSED S&T INTERVENTIONS while addressing the funding call priorities?\nMethodology: OTHER\nContribution: APPLIED\nKeywords: digital health access, youth employment, PVTG scalability, digital capacity, 100% ST, Baiga PVTG, 60% Women, Knowledge Brokers, Household surveys, regional workshops, MP Tribal Welfare Department, Health Tech Melas, Year 1 : Documentation, Year 2 : LLM / App, Year 3 : Training / Hubs, Validated IKS database, 5 operational STI Hubs, 50 Knowledge Brokers, 3 years, 90% AI accuracy, 50 youth certifications, 15,000 community users, Human - in - the - Loop, offline - first logs, quarterly surveys, Infrastructure, Capacity, Product, digital apprenticeship, voice AI, literacy gap bridge, active transmission, vs static archiving, TKDL, youth migration, 70% poverty, apprenticeship chain break, literacy - technology gap, static archives, text - heavy, oral - first culture, AI - Driven STI Hub, IKS preservation, LLM fine - tuning, Oral IK digitization, Audio documentation, Beta testing, Community hubs, Ethnobotanists, Validation, Bichhiya, Mawai, Solar power, Mobile connectivity, All - weather roads, 5 community hubs, Mandla, Train - the - Trainer, PRA - based mobilization, Bichhiya block, Mawai block, 50 Baiga youth, 50% female, ages 18 - 30, 150,000 Baiga community members, improved primary healthcare access, Mandla district, Madhya Pradesh, Government Academic Institution, capacity enhancement, IKS digitization, NEP 2020, 3 - year timeline, 200 healers, 50 youth, NHM, MoTA, Digital Empowerment Scheme, voice - enabled app, QR codes, in - person training, Llama, open - source LLM, fine - tuning, NTFP, micro - enterprises, sustainable harvesting, no conflicting information, 2026 - 05 - 16, solar infrastructure, youth broker stipends, 60 : 30 ratio, 2 Crore total, STI Hub alignment, 2 Crores, 75% Capital Assets, Infrastructure - heavy, 60 Lakhs, 30% manp