while ensuring data sovereignty remains anchored within the community.\n\nThe validation approach is iterative and deeply embedded: fifty Baiga youth Knowledge Brokers (50% female, aged 18–30), recruited through Participatory Rural Appraisal-based mobilization, will work from these hubs to audio-document the knowledge of approximately 200 traditional healers. Ethnobotanist-supervised transcription and an LLM fine-tuning loop will run continuously, with the voice-enabled mobile app beta-tested under real-world conditions. Quarterly household surveys spanning 15,000 beneficiaries and offline-first app logs will feed a human-in-the-loop review cycle, allowing the system to reach the 90% AI accuracy target for primary health queries while adapting the bilingual interface to vernacular speech patterns and dialect variation.\n\nExecution risk is systematically controlled: offline-first architecture removes connectivity as a showstopper during field use; solar power at every hub eliminates grid dependency; Prior Informed Consent and community data stewardship are enforced through Hub Advisory Circles and oversight by the MP Tribal Welfare Department; and the train-the-trainer approach builds distributed expertise so the intervention does not collapse with the departure of a single individual. The lead academic institution brings over a decade of S&T deployment experience in Mandla, the infrastructure meets DST field-site standards, and the direct involvement of the State Tribal Welfare Department provides the institutional backing needed to sustain validation across three years and later adapt the model to other PVTG blocks.	1937	DRAFT	f	1	2026-04-30 06:09:15.948	2026-04-30 06:09:15.948	2026-04-30 06:09:15.945	single_pass	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"grantDraftReadiness": {"issues": [], "warnings": []}, "grantComplianceReport": {"stage": "pass2", "passed": false, "generatedAt": "2026-04-30T06:09:15.916Z", "hardFailures": [{"key": "template_required_fact_1", "source": "temp