cmoi889wg00da40wtmkihk3v7	cmodzbetg008nxrslnjerg39y	target_population_problem_socioeconomic_status	target_population_problem_socioeconomic_status	The predominant livelihood for approximately 2,000 Phulkari artisan women in the Jalandhar region is severely hampered by inefficient manual yarn preparation, a critical bottleneck [CITE:Mamidipudi2016]. This reliance on slow, unoptimized manual processes directly restricts output, leading to persistently low wages, often below ₹5,000 per month, forcing many to abandon the craft [CITE:Dash2021]. Existing responses have failed to adequately address these fundamental production limitations within micro-clusters, often proposing fully industrial models that destroy traditional aesthetics or are unavailable to these small-scale MSMEs. This leaves artisans vulnerable to economic instability and jeopardizes the generational preservation of their rich heritage. Our proposal directly addresses this urgent socioeconomic gap by introducing context-appropriate, semi-mechanized tools.	110	\N	\N	TASK: GRANT SECTION DRAFT - STATE THE TARGET POPULATION RELATED PROBLEM YOU SEEK TO ADDRESS AND BRIEF OF THEIR SOCIO-ECONOMIC STATUS\n\nYou are writing a grant proposal section for reviewers inside Grapsi.\nWrite reviewer-facing proposal prose, not a journal manuscript section.\n\nGRANT CONTEXT:\n- Project: Grant: STI Hubs\n- Funding call: STI Hubs\n- Agency: Department of Science and Technology\n- Prep keywords: 2,000 artisans, Technology adoption, Generational preservation, Phulkari craft, MSME clusters, Scale\n\nSEEDED CONTEXT:\n- Treat this frozen workspace context as grounding. Reuse it where relevant; do not contradict it.\n- Project: Grant: STI Hubs\n- Funding call: STI Hubs\n- Agency: Department of Science and Technology\n- Deadline: 2026-05-16\n- Project duration: 3 years\n- Eligibility: The following organizations/institutes are eligible for receiving financial support for establishment of STI Hubs. Government Academic Institutions (C