rs exactly when mapped evidence is used.\n- Default to a single compact block unless the template clearly requires bullets.	Existing regional solutions for the Phulkari craft, primarily found in MSME clusters, rely on fully industrial models that often destroy traditional aesthetics . This approach is unavailable to micro-clusters and fails to address the specific needs of 2,000 marginalized women artisans, leading to slow technology adoption and a risk of abandoning the craft due to low wages. While national initiatives like the MSME SFURTI scheme aim for cluster development, they typically do not offer context-appropriate, semi-mechanized solutions tailored for traditional crafts, creating a significant technology gap. The urgency arises from the potential loss of this invaluable Indigenous Knowledge System (IKS) and the socio-economic precarity of the artisans. This proposal is justified now by its focus on developing and disseminating context-appropriate, semi-mechanized tools that respect traditional aesthetics, thereby providing a necessary baseline for why a new S&T intervention is required.	195	DRAFT	f	6	2026-04-28 06:10:00.582	2026-04-28 12:04:44.552	2026-04-28 12:04:44.545	single_pass	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"grantDraftReadiness": {"issues": [], "warnings": []}, "grantComplianceReport": {"stage": "pass2", "passed": false, "generatedAt": "2026-04-28T12:04:44.524Z", "hardFailures": [{"key": "template_required_fact_1", "source": "template", "message": "Required grant constraint is missing: Template required fact 1", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Existing regional/ National/ International solutions for the proposed problem\\"."}, {"key": "required_directly answer existing", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required point is still missing: Directly answer \\"Existing regional/ National/ International solutions for the proposed problem\\".", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Existing regional/ National/ International solutions for the proposed problem\\"."