r Local, AI - Driven, PVTG, Social Urgency, Indigenous Knowledge, medicinal plants, oral - only transmission, loss of biocultural heritage, ~200 traditional healers, last systematic documentation 1995, 70% below poverty line, 10% per year loss, fragmented NGO catalogues, inaccessible to youth, no scalable culturally sensitive tool, LLM fine - tuned, transcribed IK text, vernacular audio, bilingual modules, mobile app, query - based retrieval, adaptive learning, Baiga tribe, forest - based livelihoods, demographic details, weakest link, loss of healer knowledge, poverty, health access, minor tourism, no major manufacturing, SFURTI / ASPIRE, Maori databases, UNESCO repositories, lack oral - vernacular integration, lack youth engagement, interactive voice - based bilingual learning, advances beyond static archives, youth engagement, digitize oral IK, bilingual adaptive learning modules, voice - enabled mobile app, train 20 community trainers, establish 5 knowledge hubs, Healers, Institutional Support, Field Access, hub viability, Community brokers, Post - funding viability\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n- Return ONLY clean Markdown. No JSON, no code fences, no preamble.\n- Preserve [CITE:key] anchors exactly when mapped evidence is used.\n- Default to a single compact block unless the template clearly requires bullets.	The proposed STI Hub directly complements two national initiatives: the National Health Mission (NHM) tribal health programmes and the Ministry of Tribal Affairs (MoTA) Digital Empowerment Scheme. NHM interventions have expanded primary care outreach in Mandla’s Baiga hamlets, yet oral health knowledge and low health literacy constrain demand-side outcomes. MoTA’s scheme advances digital inclusion, but text‑heavy platforms remain inaccessible in oral‑first communities. By deploying a voice‑enabled, bilingual AI app and training 50 youth Knowledge Brokers, the Hub converts these initiatives’ infrastructure gains into measurable outcomes—improved health query resolution, validated IKS preservation, and certified digital skills for PVTG youth—while avoiding duplication and strengthening inter‑ministerial synergy.	476	DRAFT	f	1	2026-04-30 05:37:52.512	2026-04-30 05:37:52.512	2026-04-30 05:37:52.507	single_pass	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	{"grantDraftReadiness": {"issues": [], "warnings": []}, "grantComplianceReport": {"stage": "pass2", "passed": false, "generatedAt": "2026-04-30T05:37:52.486Z", "hardFailures": [{"key": "word_budget", "source": "system", "message": "Section exceeds the word budget of 100.", "ruleText": null}, {"key": "template_required_fact_1", "source": "template", "message": "Required grant constraint is missing: Template required fact 1", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Any other Government National Initiatives related to proposed activities to solve this problem\\"."}, {"key": "required_directly answer any othe", "source": "guideline", "message": "Required point is still missing: Directly answer \\"Any other Government National Initiatives related to proposed activities to solve this problem\\".", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Any other Government National Initiatives related to proposed activities to solve this problem\\"."}, {"key": "evidence_directly answer any othe", "source": "template", "message": "Required drafting evidence is missing: Directly answer \\"Any other Government National Initiatives related to proposed activities to solve this problem\\".", "ruleText": "Directly answer \\"Any other Government National Initiatives related to proposed activities to solve this problem\\"."}], "softWarnings": [], "missingEvidence": ["Directly answer \\"Any other Government National Initiatives related to proposed activities to solve this problem\\"."], "usedPrepEvidence": ["fit_and_scope:questions_other_government_initiatives"], "violatedAvoidRules": [], "unmetRequiredPoints": ["Directly answer \\"Any other Government National Initiatives related to proposed activities to solve this problem\\"."], "coveredRequi